From: devcore94 <ditternation@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: clean KernelSU config fragment

The upstream fragment contains a whitespace-only line and assigns
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS twice.  Kconfig accepts both, but emits an unexpected-data
and duplicate-symbol warning on every FloppyKernel build.  Keep the single
SUSFS assignment in the SUSFS section so the fragment remains equivalent.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/ksu.config b/arch/arm64/configs/ksu.config
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/ksu.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/ksu.config
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 ## KernelSU support config fragment
 
 CONFIG_KSU_NEXT=y
- 
 #
 # KernelSU
 #
@@ -11,8 +10,6 @@ CONFIG_KSU=y
 # CONFIG_KSU_ALLOWLIST_WORKAROUND is not set
 CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK=y
 
-CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=y
-
 #
 # KernelSU - SUSFS
 #
